# The script the fixture harness runs stepped (`fixture-test`;
# docs/dev-practices/headless-mode.md, "How the gate runs a fixture") against
# the config in `config/`, which keeps the default layout and binds
# `tab-rename` to `C-c r` and `tab-move-right` to `C-c m`; every other tab
# command is reached by the Vim scheme's own keys under `C-w`. It shows two
# tabs keeping their own windows, focus and layout, the tab bar listing
# them with the tab in view's chip in its own face, a missing tab and the
# last tab refused with the reason in the echo area. What it prints must be
# exactly `expected`. It touches no file.

reload
settle

# A frame of 640 by 480: the tiled area is 640 by 464, above the bottom row.
resize 640 480

# `C-w s` splits view 0: one tab, views 0 and 1 side by side, and no tab
# bar, since there is one tab.
key w KeyW control
key s KeyS -
scene

# `C-w c` makes a second tab after the first, on the same buffer, and
# brings it into view: view 2 alone in the tiled area, now 640 by 448, and
# the tab bar's view last, in the strip above the bottom row, its second
# chip in `tab-bar.selected`.
key w KeyW control
key c KeyC -
scene

# `C-w s C-w z` splits view 2 and zooms the new window: the second tab
# shows one view.
key w KeyW control
key s KeyS -
key w KeyW control
key z KeyZ -
scene

# `C-w p` goes back to the first tab, as it was left: views 0 and 1 side by
# side, the focus on view 1, and the first chip selected.
key w KeyW control
key p KeyP -
scene

# `C-w n` goes to the second tab, still zoomed, its focus where it was.
key w KeyW control
key n KeyN -
scene

# `C-w 3` is refused: there is no tab 3.
key w KeyW control
key 3 Digit3 -
scene

# `C-c r`, `notes` and `<Enter>` rename the second tab: its chip reads
# `notes`.
key c KeyC control
key r KeyR -
commit notes
key <Enter> Enter -
scene

# `C-c m` on the last tab moves nothing.
key c KeyC control
key m KeyM -
scene

# `C-w w`, `1` and `<Enter>` switch to tab 1.
key w KeyW control
key w KeyW -
commit 1
key <Enter> Enter -
scene

# `C-w &` closes the first tab: the second, `notes`, zoomed, is left alone,
# and the bar goes.
key w KeyW control
key & Digit7 shift
scene

# `C-w &` again is refused: the last tab cannot be closed.
key w KeyW control
key & Digit7 shift
scene
